# How a logic module is compiled into the native plugin (platform/logic_native.cpp, its own
# translation unit). Read by CMakeLists.txt and tools/test-budget.sh: every line that starts
# with a dash is one flag. docs/midi-tools.md, "The step budget"; decision 46.
#
# The step budget: every edge of the module's code calls __sanitizer_cov_trace_pc_guard
# (PangeaLogicGuard.h), which counts it and watches the stack. no-prune keeps the call on
# blocks that loop to themselves; without -fno-finite-loops clang may delete a loop that
# never ends instead of keeping it, and the budget could not stop it.
-fsanitize-coverage=trace-pc-guard,no-prune
-fno-finite-loops
# The same rounding as WebAssembly: no fused multiply-add (Two Hands' gold test).
-ffp-contract=off
# As in WebAssembly: no exceptions, no run-time types. A stopped call leaves through
# _longjmp, so a function-local static must not hold a lock while it is being made.
-fno-exceptions
-fno-rtti
-fno-threadsafe-statics
# What a budget cannot stop, refused when it compiles: a stack that grows by a run-time
# amount, a frame too large for an audio thread, and code that runs when the plugin loads
# or unloads, outside any budget. The server compiles with the same refusals.
-Werror=vla
-Wframe-larger-than=16384
-Werror=frame-larger-than
-Werror=global-constructors
-Werror=exit-time-destructors
